WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.517
The first major question is how the dataset is organized.

00:00:03.517 --> 00:00:06.587
Structured data follows a predefined schema.

00:00:06.587 --> 00:00:12.077
Semi-structured data has named fields but allows flexibility and nesting.

00:00:12.077 --> 00:00:17.032
Unstructured data does not naturally arrive as rows and columns.

00:00:17.032 --> 00:00:19.982
These categories describe organization.

00:00:19.982 --> 00:00:26.772
A structured table can still have missing values, duplicate records, or poorly defined variables.

00:00:26.772 --> 00:00:30.142
Organization and quality are separate issues.

00:00:30.142 --> 00:00:36.937
Connect this idea to a hospital combining patient tables, device JSON, and clinical notes.

00:00:36.937 --> 00:00:42.362
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:49.782
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:49.782 --> 00:00:55.632
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:55.632 --> 00:01:01.978
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
